{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G9E4UtNB9aBehswfzkZ8Aj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment data for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment plan, under the \"best\" tier definition they've provided. I need to produce expected results with rationales for each planned experiment, all consistent with the best-tier metrics and narrative.\n\nLet me go through each planned experiment and generate the data.\n\nKey best-tier parameters:\n- libero_plus_overall_meta_brain: [76, 82]\n- gain_over_frozen: [22, 28]\n- universal_lora_overall: [63, 66]\n\n\n- gain_over_universal_lora: [10, 18]\n- per_type_specialization_delta_max: [12, 25]\n- oracle_par_gap: [0, 2]\n- routing_diagonality: [0.85, 0.98]\n- gain_per_million_params: [3.7, 4.7]\n- cm_ablation_delta: [1, 4]\n\nWith the frozen pi0 baseline at 53.6%, a gain of 22-28 points puts Meta-Brain in the 76-82 range, which aligns with the overall performance target.\n\nNow I'm working through the specific performance tiers. Universal LoRA sits around 64.8%, and Meta-Brain with PAR reaches 78.4%, giving a gain of 13.6 points over universal LoRA. This falls within the expected 10-18 range, and the oracle routing gap of 1.2 points stays within the 0-2 bound, confirming the numbers are internally consistent.\n\nFor the per-perturbation analysis on LIBERO-Plus, I need to establish baseline performance across the seven perturbation types: camera, light, background, noise, layout, robot, and clean. I'm constructing reasonable frozen pi0 numbers based on typical VLA degradation patterns, where camera and layout tend to show different sensitivity levels compared to visual perturbations like noise and background. I'm trying to figure out whether LIBERO-Plus uses 6 or 7 perturbation types. The explicit list shows camera, light, background, noise, layout, and robot, but the paper mentions 7 types total, so there might be an additional category I'm missing or a clean baseline included. I'm settling on 6 perturbation types across 3 categories and need to work out the numbers so they average to around 53.6% for the frozen baseline. Let me adjust the per-type performance metrics to hit that target.\n\nNow I'm calculating the universal LoRA improvements, where each perturbation type gets a boost—mostly around 10 percentage points, though physical perturbations might see slightly larger gains from the general training approach. Now I'm setting up the Meta-Brain routing with specialized LoRA experts for each perturbation type, targeting around 78.4% overall performance where each expert shows meaningful gains on their specialty compared to the universal baseline. Now I'm looking at how each specialized LoRA performs on its own domain versus cross-domain tasks. The visual expert shows strong gains on camera, light, background, and noise types—ranging from +14 to +20 percentage points above the universal baseline—but struggles significantly on spatial and physical tasks, dropping 18-20 points below universal performance. I need to compile the same breakdown for the spatial and physical experts to see the full specialization trade-off pattern. good, the specialization delta is within the target range. Now I'm mapping out the planned experiments—LoRA expert training to validate per-type performance, Meta-Brain assembly to measure overall gains and routing behavior, Oracle routing to establish the theoretical ceiling, and an ablation ladder showing the progression from frozen baseline through universal to Meta-Brain to oracle. I'm also planning to reproduce FTM results to confirm it excels on visual tasks but doesn't help with spatial or physical reasoning, plus a parameter efficiency analysis to quantify the gains per million parameters.\n\nNow I'm checking the Meta-Brain + CM experiment—if the base system hits 78.4% and adding contrastive matching pushes it to 80.8%, that's a 2.4 point gain. But I need to clarify whether the 78.4 baseline already includes CM or not. Looking at the baselines, Meta-Brain without CM is around 6M parameters, and with CM it's 6M plus 1M, so they're separate configurations. The overall range for Meta-Brain is [76, 82], which suggests there's some variance depending on the exact setup. I'm working through the exact numbers for Meta-Brain's performance metrics. The headline ~78% likely refers to the full system with CM included, so I should set that as the main result and work backward to establish the ablation delta and baseline performance without CM. Now I'm mapping out the performance hierarchy across different routing and modulation approaches. Meta-Brain with PAR routing alone hits 76.0%, and adding the CM modulation pushes it to 78.4%. Oracle routing—which uses perfect ground truth labels instead of PAR—should theoretically perform better, so I'm working through whether oracle with CM reaches around 80.0% while oracle without CM sits at 77.8%. R without CM... and CM adds modulation on top. Let me think about this differently.\n\nOracle routing = ground truth type → LoRA expert. This is the ceiling for routing quality.\nPAR routing = learned router → LoRA expert. Any gap is due to routing errors.\n\nOracle routing should give the upper bound for the LoRA bank performance. CM is orthogonal — it modulates routing weights based on retrieved exemplars.\n\nSo the performance ladder looks like: Frozen at 53.6%, Universal LoRA at 64.8%, Meta-Brain with PAR routing at 78.4%, Oracle routing at 79.6% (only 1.2% above PAR), and with CM applied we get 80.8% and 82.0% respectively. The CM delta checks out at 2.4 percentage points.\n\nFor the ablation study, Meta-Brain represents the full system with PAR routing and the 3-LoRA bank, while CM is a separate orthogonal ablation. The gains over frozen are 24.8 percentage points, and I'm verifying the gains over universal LoRA as well.\n\nFor the headline, Meta-Brain at 78.4% closes about 90% of the gap to VLA-GSE's 81.2%, which is a strong positioning story.\n\nWith the corrected CM adjustment of 1.8%, Meta-Brain+CM reaches 80.2% and closes 96.4% of that gap — nearly matching VLA-GSE's performance while using 20x fewer parameters, which definitely qualifies as best-tier competitive.\n\nNow I'm thinking through plan_009 and the router approach.  The attention-based router edges out the simpler alternatives with 97.6% routing accuracy translating to 78.6% downstream, but the marginal improvement doesn't warrant the added complexity. For plan_010, comparing 3-class versus 6-class routing shows that three experts are sufficient — the 0.8% gain from doubling to six experts amounts to only 0.27% per additional expert, so the extra parameters aren't justified. I need to evaluate plan_011 and plan_012 next to see how cross-backbone and layer placement decisions affect the overall architecture.\n\nLooking at the cross-backbone experiments with SmolVLA and OpenVLA, I'm seeing Phase 0 F1 scores above 0.96 on the second backbone with an 18-22% gain over the frozen baseline, which confirms the approach generalizes well. For layer placement, the ablations show clear patterns — LoRA-V performs best on early layers for Visual types, LoRA-S on mid layers for Spatial, and LoRA-P on late layers for Physical, though applying all layers gets close to optimal at the cost of more parameters.\n\nNow I'm checking the efficiency metrics: Meta-Brain achieves 4.13 gain per million parameters, which falls nicely within the target range of 3.7 to 4.7. For routing diagonality, I need to verify that the routing weights maintain near-diagonal structure in the 0.85 to 0.98 range, meaning Visual inputs should route primarily to Visual experts.\n\nI'm now compiling the per-perturbation performance numbers for the full YAML output, looking at direct evaluations where each expert handles its own perturbation type and cross-type mismatches to get the complete performance picture. Looking at the specialization delta more carefully—it's actually measured at the individual perturbation type level, not the category level. Camera shows the biggest gap with LoRA-V hitting 74% versus universal's 54%, giving a 20% delta, which fits the target range. Now I'm comparing FTM performance on the visual perturbations, where it specializes: it averages around 71.5% across camera, light, background, and noise, performing nearly as well as LoRA-V on camera but showing weaker results on the spatial types like layout and robot.\n\nThe interesting part is that Meta-Brain actually outperforms FTM overall at 78.4% despite FTM being designed specifically for visual perturbations. Even on visual alone, Meta-Brain edges ahead at 74% average versus FTM's 71.5%, though FTM does this with far fewer parameters—just 4K compared to LoRA-V's 2M. The paper claims FTM hits 90% on visual perturbations, but that's on their original benchmark, not our pi0 setup, so the reproduced results here are more realistic for this particular configuration.\n\nNow I'm looking at the parameter efficiency trade-offs. Meta-Brain with 6M parameters achieves a gain of 24.8 points per million parameters, while Universal LoRA at 2M gets 5.6 points per million. FTM's advantage is its extreme efficiency on visual—it gains about 24.5 points on visual alone with just 0.004M parameters, though it struggles significantly on spatial and physical reasoning tasks, bringing its overall performance down to around 68.7%.\n\nFor VLA-GSE, I need to be careful about the baseline comparison since it uses a different backbone than the others. The paper shows it reaches 81.2% compared to LoRA's 69.2%, but I should calculate its gain relative to its own frozen baseline rather than mixing baselines across different models.\n\nAssuming VLA-GSE's frozen performance is around 56%, that gives a gain of about 25.2 percentage points, which translates to roughly 0.22 gain per million parameters. Meta-Brain, by contrast, achieves 4.13 gain per million parameters—about 19 times more efficient, which matches the \"20x fewer parameters\" claim from the paper.\n\nNow I have the data I need to compile the full YAML structure.\n\nI should focus on the planned experiments—plan_002 through plan_012—since plan_001 is already running with actual metrics. For each one, I'll need detailed per-perturbation breakdowns and thorough result rationales. Let me start drafting the comprehensive YAML with all the planned experiments included.\n\nLooking at the router comparison in plan_009, the MLP architecture strikes the right balance—it achieves nearly the same downstream performance as attention-based routing but with much simpler implementation, while the linear approach lags noticeably behind. For plan_010, the 3-class taxonomy is already well-validated in the best tier, so the modest 1% improvement from moving to 6-class granularity suggests we're not leaving much on the table. In plan_011, I'm using OpenVLA as the second backbone to test cross-architecture generalization, with the Phase 0 F1 score at 0.972.\n\nThe OpenVLA results show Meta-Brain delivers a 20.4% improvement over the frozen baseline on LIBERO-Plus, which validates the approach works across different backbones. For plan_012, the layer placement analysis reveals each modality has its optimal range—visual features benefit most from layers 2-8, spatial from 6-12, and physical from 10-16—but applying LoRA across all layers performs nearly as well, suggesting the default PaliGemma configuration is already close to optimal. I've got enough data now to synthesize the full findings.\n\nActually, let me verify the per-distraction numbers for Meta-Brain are internally consistent. The frozen pi0 baseline checks out at 53.6% overall, and the universal LoRA configuration averages to about 64.8%, but I need to confirm the Meta-Brain results align across these different experimental conditions.\n\nLooking at the Meta-Brain with PAR but no contrastive matching, I'm getting 78.4% overall, which is about 1.2 points below the oracle performance. When I add contrastive matching on top, the improvement is around 2 points, bringing it to 80.4%. Let me see if I can adjust the per-distraction values slightly to hit exactly 2.4 points of improvement instead. Now I'm verifying the routing weights make sense—for a 3-class expert system, each input type should route most heavily to its corresponding LoRA module, and the average diagonality of 0.92 confirms that's happening correctly across visual, spatial, and physical perturbations.\n\nI need to structure the comprehensive YAML with all the experiment metadata including names, descriptions, expected results with their values, rationales, and supporting tables and figures. Since plan_005 has 5 seeds, I'll need to calculate standard deviations for those metrics. I'm also working through the efficiency calculations for the scatter plot—Meta-Brain achieves about 4.13 gain per million parameters while Universal LoRA gets higher per-parameter efficiency at 5.55 but with much lower absolute gains.\n\nFor FTM, the 4K parameter count creates an extreme per-parameter ratio that's somewhat misleading since it only improves visual performance, so I'll focus on the overall gain metric for the scatter plot comparison instead.\n\nNow I'm looking at the final numbers across all approaches: FTM shows 15.1 overall gain with minimal parameters, FLA achieves around 18 gain with 4.7M parameters, and I need to verify the plan_005 results with their confidence intervals across the five seeds to ensure accuracy before writing this up. I'm finishing the delta calculations—the max specialization advantage is 20.0 from the camera type, which fits the expected range. Now I need to account for soft routing in Meta-Brain's performance: with a routing diagonality of 0.92, about 91% of visual inputs route to LoRA-V while 9% leaks to the other experts, so I should adjust those numbers to reflect the weighted average rather than pure LoRA-V performance. Generating YAML experiment data...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11192,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11192},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40703030-3e58-41b3-9b6d-2da547bf07b9","uuid":"31577a15-7b6b-439e-830a-310759c014aa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G9E4UtNB9aBehswfzkZ8Aj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Original framing holds as-is. Headline: Meta-Brain achieves 78.4% on LIBERO-Plus \n  with 6M params (80.8% with CM), closing 90% of the gap to VLA-GSE (81.2%, 114M params) \n  at 19x fewer trainable parameters. All three claims land cleanly — Phase 0 diagnosability \n  enables zero-overhead routing (Claim 1), the ablation ladder shows targeted > uniform \n  correction with 13.6% gain over universal LoRA (Claim 2), and the parameter efficiency \n  scatter plot positions Meta-Brain at 4.13 gain/M-param vs VLA-GSE's 0.24 (Claim 3). \n  Specialization is validated by 20% max delta (camera type) and strong cross-type \n  degradation of mismatched experts. Oracle-PAR gap of 1.2% confirms Phase 0 signal is \n  actionable. Paper should lead with the ablation ladder figure and close with the \n  parameter-efficiency scatter plot.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"LoRA expert training — 3 specialized + 1 universal\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      Train 4 LoRA adapters (rank 16) on frozen pi0 PaliGemma layers: LoRA-V (Visual), \n      LoRA-S (Spatial), LoRA-P (Physical), Universal LoRA (mixed). Evaluate each on \n      own-type and cross-type perturbations.\n    expected_results:\n      lora_v_visual_avg: 76.0\n      lora_v_camera: 74.0\n      lora_v_light: 80.0\n      lora_v_background: 78.0\n      lora_v_noise: 72.0\n      lora_v_on_spatial: 60.0\n      lora_v_on_physical: 54.0\n      lora_s_layout: 90.0\n      lora_s_on_visual_avg: 46.5\n      lora_s_on_physical: 56.0\n      lora_p_robot: 88.0\n      lora_p_on_visual_avg: 44.0\n      lora_p_on_spatial: 62.0\n      universal_lora_overall: 64.8\n      universal_camera: 54.0\n      universal_light: 66.0\n      universal_background: 62.0\n      universal_noise: 54.0\n      universal_layout: 78.0\n      universal_robot: 74.0\n      per_type_specialization_delta_max: 20.0\n      per_type_specialization_delta_min: 12.0\n      cross_type_degradation_max: -20.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Rank-16 LoRA on PaliGemma layers provides足够的修正容量处理单一扰动类型。\n      专用 LoRA 在其目标类型上大幅超越 universal LoRA（最大 delta=20%，camera 类型），因为：\n      (1) Visual 扰动主要破坏 PaliGemma 早期视觉编码，LoRA-V 的全部容量用于修复这一信号通路，\n      而 universal LoRA 必须将同样容量分摊到三类截然不同的校正模式上；\n      (2) Spatial (layout) 扰动修改物体空间关系，LoRA-S 学到的校正向量直接对齐中层空间表征，\n      在 layout 上达 90%——这是所有组合中最高的，因为 layout 是单一子类、分布集中；\n      (3) Physical (robot) 扰动改变力学属性，LoRA-P 在 robot 上达 88%。\n      Cross-type 严重退化（LoRA-V 在 physical 仅 54%，低于 frozen baseline 的 56%）证实\n      三类扰动所需的校正模式确实互不兼容——这是 Claim 2 的关键论据：专用路由并非锦上添花，\n      而是必要条件。Universal LoRA 在 64.8% 饱和，因为 rank-16 的有限容量在三类矛盾梯度\n      方向间折衷，导致每种类型都欠校正。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Expert cross-evaluation matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Expert\", \"camera\", \"light\", \"background\", \"noise\", \"layout\", \"robot\", \"Overall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA-V\", 74.0, 80.0, 78.0, 72.0, 60.0, 54.0, 69.7]\n          - [\"LoRA-S\", 44.0, 52.0, 48.0, 42.0, 90.0, 56.0, 55.3]\n          - [\"LoRA-P\", 40.0, 50.0, 46.0, 40.0, 62.0, 88.0, 54.3]\n          - [\"Universal\", 54.0, 66.0, 62.0, 54.0, 78.0, 74.0, 64.8]\n          - [\"Frozen pi0\", 42.0, 58.0, 52.0, 46.0, 68.0, 56.0, 53.6]\n      - name: \"Specialization delta (own-type expert minus universal)\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation type\", \"Specialist\", \"Universal\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 74.0, 54.0, \"+20.0\"]\n          - [\"light\", 80.0, 66.0, \"+14.0\"]\n          - [\"background\", 78.0, 62.0, \"+16.0\"]\n          - [\"noise\", 72.0, 54.0, \"+18.0\"]\n          - [\"layout\", 90.0, 78.0, \"+12.0\"]\n          - [\"robot\", 88.0, 74.0, \"+14.0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×6 cross-evaluation matrix (expert rows × perturbation columns), strong diagonal blocks visible — LoRA-V hot on left 4 columns, LoRA-S hot on layout, LoRA-P hot on robot. Off-diagonal cells cool/cold, many below frozen baseline.\"\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: per-type success rate for each expert + universal + frozen, clearly showing each specialist dominates its own types while failing on others.\"\n    analysis: >\n      最核心发现：cross-type 退化的幅度（最大 -20% vs frozen）与 own-type 提升幅度（最大 +20%）\n      几乎对称，说明 LoRA 学到的不是通用「鲁棒性」而是类型特异的校正映射。\n      Universal LoRA 在每个类型上都不如对应专家，差距最大的是 camera（-20）和 noise（-18），\n      最小的是 layout（-12）。Layout 差距最小因为它是 Spatial 类的唯一子类型，universal LoRA \n      分配给 spatial 校正的有效容量比例相对较高。这为 Meta-Brain 的路由设计提供了直接动机：\n      如果能正确识别扰动类型并激活对应专家，就能同时获得所有类型上的最优校正。\n\n  - name: \"Meta-Brain assembly — PAR + LoRA bank E2E\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      Assemble PAR router (PaliGemma layer 6 MLP) + 3 frozen LoRA experts with soft routing. \n      Fine-tune only PAR routing weights end-to-end on LIBERO-Plus rollouts.\n    expected_results:\n      libero_plus_overall: 78.4\n      camera: 72.0\n      light: 78.0\n      background: 76.0\n      noise: 70.0\n      layout: 88.0\n      robot: 86.0\n      visual_avg: 74.0\n      spatial_avg: 88.0\n      physical_avg: 86.0\n      routing_diagonality: 0.92\n      par_visual_weight_on_lora_v: 0.91\n      par_spatial_weight_on_lora_s: 0.93\n      par_physical_weight_on_lora_p: 0.92\n      trainable_params_M: 6.1\n      routing_params_K: 48\n      gain_over_frozen: 24.8\n      gain_over_universal_lora: 13.6\n    result_rationale: >\n      PAR router 利用 Phase 0 已验证的 layer 6 激活信号（F1=0.993）进行软路由，\n      routing diagonality 达到 0.92 意味着 92% 的权重正确分配给目标专家。\n      剩余 8% 的\"泄漏\"实际上是有益的：\n      (1) 部分扰动（如 background clutter + 轻微 layout shift 同时出现）需要混合校正；\n      (2) soft routing 的平滑梯度使得 PAR 在 E2E fine-tuning 中可以学到比 hard routing \n      更精细的权重配置。\n      整体 78.4% 低于各专家在 own-type 上的最优成绩的加权平均（~81%），差距来源：\n      (a) 8% 路由泄漏导致部分样本获得次优校正；\n      (b) PAR fine-tuning 只调路由权重、冻结 LoRA，整体达不到联合训练的上界。\n      但 78.4% 已经比 universal LoRA 高 13.6%，证明路由带来的专家选择增益远超路由误差成本。\n      layout 和 robot 达到 88% 和 86%（接近 oracle 的 plan_002 数据），因为这两类是 \n      单一子类型、PAR 分类难度最低。Visual 子类型（camera 72%、noise 70%）相对低一些，\n      因为 4 种视觉扰动之间存在一定混淆（noise vs camera 的 PAR 权重偶尔偏移）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Meta-Brain per-perturbation breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"Frozen\", \"Universal\", \"Meta-Brain\", \"Gain vs Frozen\", \"Gain vs Universal\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 42.0, 54.0, 72.0, \"+30.0\", \"+18.0\"]\n          - [\"light\", 58.0, 66.0, 78.0, \"+20.0\", \"+12.0\"]\n          - [\"background\", 52.0, 62.0, 76.0, \"+24.0\", \"+14.0\"]\n          - [\"noise\", 46.0, 54.0, 70.0, \"+24.0\", \"+16.0\"]\n          - [\"layout\", 68.0, 78.0, 88.0, \"+20.0\", \"+10.0\"]\n          - [\"robot\", 56.0, 74.0, 86.0, \"+30.0\", \"+12.0\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 53.6, 64.8, 78.4, \"+24.8\", \"+13.6\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Architecture diagram: Frozen pi0 → PaliGemma layer 6 → PAR MLP → [p_V, p_S, p_P] soft weights → LoRA-V/S/P bank → h_corrected = h_frozen + Σ p_k·LoRA_k(h). Only PAR weights are trainable (48K params), LoRA experts frozen from plan_002.\"\n      - \"Routing weight heatmap: 3×3 matrix (perturbation category × expert), near-diagonal with 0.91-0.93 on diagonal, 0.03-0.05 off-diagonal. Color-coded to show PAR correctly identifies perturbation type.\"\n      - \"Per-perturbation grouped bar chart: 6 clusters (one per type), 3 bars each (frozen/universal/meta-brain), showing consistent improvement across all types.\"\n    analysis: >\n      13.6% gain over universal LoRA 是 Claim 2 的核心数值。在参数量相同（6M = 3×2M \n      vs 1×2M + 相同总 rank budget 的另一种分配）甚至 Meta-Brain 用了 3 倍参数的情况下，\n      关键洞察不是「更多参数 = 更好」而是「路由后的容量利用率远高于混合训练」。\n      可做公平对比：rank-48 universal LoRA（与 3×rank-16 参数量相当）预期仍然饱和在 ~67%，\n      因为高 rank 并不能解决梯度冲突——这是 plan_005 ablation ladder 要验证的。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle routing ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      Replace PAR with ground-truth perturbation labels for hard routing. \n      Measures upper bound for routing quality.\n    expected_results:\n      oracle_overall: 79.6\n      oracle_camera: 74.0\n      oracle_light: 78.0\n      oracle_background: 78.0\n      oracle_noise: 72.0\n      oracle_layout: 88.0\n      oracle_robot: 88.0\n      oracle_par_gap: 1.2\n      oracle_par_gap_camera: 2.0\n      oracle_par_gap_light: 0.0\n      oracle_par_gap_background: 2.0\n      oracle_par_gap_noise: 2.0\n      oracle_par_gap_layout: 0.0\n      oracle_par_gap_robot: 2.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Oracle-PAR gap 仅 1.2%，直接证明 Phase 0 的分类信号在下游任务中是 actionable 的。\n      Gap 主要来自 Visual 子类型（camera +2, background +2, noise +2），因为 PAR 在 \n      4 种 Visual 子类型间存在少量混淆（~8% 路由泄漏），导致部分 Visual 样本获得了 \n      LoRA-S/P 的轻微干扰。Layout 和 robot 的 gap 为 0-2%，因为这两类在 Phase 0 \n      的分类准确率接近 100%（单一子类型、特征空间高度分离）。\n      1.2% gap 远小于 Meta-Brain vs Universal LoRA 的 13.6% gain，这意味着即使路由 \n      有少量误差，路由策略本身的收益也远大于误差带来的损失。\n      Oracle 79.6% 低于各专家 own-type 最优的简单加权平均（~81%），因为 oracle routing \n      是 hard routing（1-hot 权重），丢失了 soft routing 在某些混合扰动样本上的 \n      blending 优势。这也解释了为什么 PAR 的 soft routing 在某些类型上能接近 oracle。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Oracle vs PAR per-perturbation gap\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"PAR\", \"Oracle\", \"Gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 72.0, 74.0, 2.0]\n          - [\"light\", 78.0, 78.0, 0.0]\n          - [\"background\", 76.0, 78.0, 2.0]\n          - [\"noise\", 70.0, 72.0, 2.0]\n          - [\"layout\", 88.0, 88.0, 0.0]\n          - [\"robot\", 86.0, 88.0, 2.0]\n          - [\"Overall\", 78.4, 79.6, 1.2]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: PAR vs Oracle per perturbation type, gap annotations on top. Visual types show small consistent gaps; Spatial/Physical nearly identical.\"\n    analysis: >\n      1.2% gap 是对 reviewer concern C1（「Phase 0 分类太简单，路由无用」）的最佳回应：\n      分类简单 ≠ 路由无价值。分类简单意味着路由几乎免费获得正确性（zero overhead），\n      而 13.6% 的 gain over universal 证明路由的价值在于下游校正，不在路由本身的难度。\n      Oracle gap 小反而是优势——说明 PAR 已经接近天花板，无需更复杂的路由器。\n\n  - name: \"Ablation ladder — Frozen → Universal → Meta-Brain → Oracle\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic comparison on LIBERO-Plus with 5 seeds. Core evidence for Claim 2.\n    expected_results:\n      frozen_mean: 53.6\n      frozen_std: 1.4\n      universal_mean: 64.8\n      universal_std: 1.8\n      meta_brain_mean: 78.4\n      meta_brain_std: 1.6\n      oracle_mean: 79.6\n      oracle_std: 1.2\n      gain_frozen_to_universal: 11.2\n      gain_universal_to_meta_brain: 13.6\n      gain_meta_brain_to_oracle: 1.2\n      gain_frozen_to_meta_brain: 24.8\n      p_value_universal_vs_meta_brain: 0.0003\n      p_value_meta_brain_vs_oracle: 0.14\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-seed 统计验证下，ablation ladder 呈现清晰的三级阶梯：\n      (1) Frozen→Universal (+11.2%): universal LoRA 提供了基础的扰动鲁棒性，\n      证明 PaliGemma 层的 LoRA adaptation 是有效的校正机制。标准差 1.8% 较高，\n      因为 universal LoRA 在不同 seed 下对不同扰动类型的容量分配方式不稳定（\n      有时偏重 visual、有时偏重 spatial），导致 run-to-run 方差较大。\n      (2) Universal→Meta-Brain (+13.6%, p<0.001): 路由带来的增益甚至超过 universal LoRA \n      自身 over frozen 的增益，统计显著。这是 Claim 2 最强的证据——同样的 LoRA capacity，\n      路由后的利用效率比混合使用高出一倍以上。Meta-Brain 的标准差 1.6% 低于 universal \n      的 1.8%，因为路由机制减少了容量分配的随机性。\n      (3) Meta-Brain→Oracle (+1.2%, p=0.14): 差异不显著，证明 PAR 路由已接近上界。\n      这一不显著结果本身就是积极信号——说明无需 oracle 标签，Phase 0 分类足矣。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Ablation ladder summary (5 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Params\", \"Overall ± std\", \"Gain over Frozen\", \"Gain over Prev. Step\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Frozen pi0\", \"0\", \"53.6 ± 1.4\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Universal LoRA (r16)\", \"~2M\", \"64.8 ± 1.8\", \"+11.2\", \"+11.2\"]\n          - [\"Meta-Brain (PAR+ALB)\", \"~6M\", \"78.4 ± 1.6\", \"+24.8\", \"+13.6\"]\n          - [\"Oracle routing\", \"~6M\", \"79.6 ± 1.2\", \"+26.0\", \"+1.2\"]\n      - name: \"Per-perturbation ablation (mean over 5 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"Frozen\", \"Universal\", \"Meta-Brain\", \"Oracle\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 42.0, 54.0, 72.0, 74.0]\n          - [\"light\", 58.0, 66.0, 78.0, 78.0]\n          - [\"background\", 52.0, 62.0, 76.0, 78.0]\n          - [\"noise\", 46.0, 54.0, 70.0, 72.0]\n          - [\"layout\", 68.0, 78.0, 88.0, 88.0]\n          - [\"robot\", 56.0, 74.0, 86.0, 88.0]\n          - [\"Overall\", 53.6, 64.8, 78.4, 79.6]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart (Figure 4 in paper): 4 bars per perturbation type + overall, ascending Frozen→Universal→Meta-Brain→Oracle. Error bars from 5 seeds. Clear staircase pattern; biggest jump is Universal→Meta-Brain.\"\n      - \"Delta decomposition stacked bar: overall gain 26.0% (oracle over frozen) decomposed into universal contribution (11.2), routing contribution (13.6), routing-perfection headroom (1.2).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Ablation ladder 的核心叙事：从 frozen 到 oracle 的 26.0% 总增益中，\n      routing 贡献了 13.6%（52%），universal adaptation 贡献了 11.2%（43%），\n      routing 精度 headroom 仅 1.2%（5%）。这意味着 perturbation-diagnostic routing \n      不是边际优化，而是与 LoRA adaptation 本身同等量级的增益来源。\n      统计显著性分析确认 universal→meta-brain 的增益是 robust 的（p<0.001），\n      而 meta-brain→oracle 的差异不显著（p=0.14），为 PAR 路由的实用性提供了严格支持。\n\n  - name: \"FTM/FLA reproduction on pi0\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      Reproduce FTM on pi0 for visual perturbations. Compare with Meta-Brain on visual \n      and demonstrate Meta-Brain's advantage on non-visual types.\n    expected_results:\n      ftm_camera: 70.0\n      ftm_light: 76.0\n      ftm_background: 72.0\n      ftm_noise: 68.0\n      ftm_visual_avg: 71.5\n      ftm_layout: 68.0\n      ftm_robot: 56.0\n      ftm_overall: 68.3\n      ftm_params_K: 4\n      meta_brain_visual_avg: 74.0\n      meta_brain_advantage_visual: 2.5\n      meta_brain_advantage_overall: 10.1\n      meta_brain_advantage_non_visual: 22.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      FTM 在 pi0 上的复现结果合理偏低于原论文（原论文用不同 backbone 且只报告视觉扰动）。\n      FTM 在 visual 子类型上达 71.5%（接近 LoRA-V 的 76.0%），说明 FTM 的 feature \n      modulation 策略确实能有效修复视觉损坏——这与 FTM 原论文的结论一致。\n      但 FTM 在 layout (68.0%) 和 robot (56.0%) 上几乎无增益或低于 universal LoRA，\n      因为 FTM 的设计假设扰动仅存在于视觉通道，其 modulation 无法处理空间关系和物理属性的变化。\n      Meta-Brain 在 visual 上略优于 FTM (+2.5%)，因为 LoRA-V 有更多参数（2M vs 4K）\n      可以学到更精细的校正。关键差异在非 visual 类型：Meta-Brain 在 layout+robot 上\n      平均 87.0% vs FTM 的 62.0%（+25.0%），这 25% 的差距直接论证了多类型校正的必要性。\n      FTM 的 4K 参数量在 per-param visual gain 上极其高效，但 scope-limited——\n      这在 parameter efficiency scatter plot (plan_007) 中会成为一个有趣的数据点。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"FTM vs Meta-Brain comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"FTM (4K)\", \"Meta-Brain (6M)\", \"LoRA-V (2M)\", \"Universal (2M)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 70.0, 72.0, 74.0, 54.0]\n          - [\"light\", 76.0, 78.0, 80.0, 66.0]\n          - [\"background\", 72.0, 76.0, 78.0, 62.0]\n          - [\"noise\", 68.0, 70.0, 72.0, 54.0]\n          - [\"layout\", 68.0, 88.0, 60.0, 78.0]\n          - [\"robot\", 56.0, 86.0, 54.0, 74.0]\n          - [\"Overall\", 68.3, 78.4, 69.7, 64.8]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart: 6 axes (perturbation types), overlaid polygons for FTM/Meta-Brain/Universal. FTM polygon inflated in left 4 axes (visual) but deflated in right 2 (spatial/physical); Meta-Brain polygon uniformly large.\"\n    analysis: >\n      FTM 是一个重要的 baseline，因为它代表了「单模态专家」的最佳案例。\n      Meta-Brain 的价值主张不是在任何单一类型上打败 FTM，而是在所有类型上同时提供 \n      强大校正——这正是 perturbation-diagnostic routing 的设计目标。\n      在论文中应将 FTM 定位为「visual-only routing 的上界参考」，\n      并强调 Meta-Brain 的 multi-type coverage 是其独特贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Parameter efficiency analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      Compute gain-over-frozen per method, normalize by trainable params. \n      Generate scatter plot (x=params, y=gain). Core visual evidence for Claim 3.\n    expected_results:\n      meta_brain_gain: 24.8\n      meta_brain_params_M: 6.1\n      meta_brain_gain_per_M: 4.07\n      meta_brain_with_cm_gain: 27.2\n      meta_brain_with_cm_params_M: 6.1\n      meta_brain_with_cm_gain_per_M: 4.46\n      universal_lora_gain: 11.2\n      universal_lora_params_M: 2.0\n      universal_lora_gain_per_M: 5.60\n      ftm_gain_overall: 14.7\n      ftm_params_M: 0.004\n      ftm_gain_per_M: 3675.0\n      vla_gse_gain: 27.6\n      vla_gse_params_M: 114.0\n      vla_gse_gain_per_M: 0.24\n      meta_brain_vs_vla_gse_param_ratio: 18.7\n      meta_brain_vs_vla_gse_gain_ratio: 0.90\n      meta_brain_pareto_optimal: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Meta-Brain 的 gain/M-param = 4.07，是 VLA-GSE (0.24) 的 17 倍。\n      在 scatter plot 上 Meta-Brain 位于 Pareto 前沿的关键位置：\n      (1) 相比 VLA-GSE：以 5.3% 的参数量达到 90% 的 gain，参数效率高 17x；\n      (2) 相比 Universal LoRA：gain/M 虽低（4.07 vs 5.60），但绝对 gain 高 13.6%，\n      说明 3x 参数扩展用于路由（而非增大 rank）是高效的；\n      (3) 相比 FTM：FTM 的 per-param efficiency 极高（3675 gain/M）但绝对 gain \n      受限于 visual-only scope，在 scatter plot 上位于右下角「高效率低总量」区域。\n      这三对比较构成 Claim 3 的完整论证：Meta-Brain 在「参数-增益」trade-off \n      空间中占据了 VLA-GSE 和 FTM 之间的最优区间。\n      VLA-GSE 的 gain 数据直接引自原论文（Qwen3-VL-4B backbone 上 frozen 53.6%→81.2%，\n      gain=27.6%），跨 backbone 比较需在论文中注明 caveat。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Parameter efficiency comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Backbone\", \"Trainable Params\", \"Gain over Frozen\", \"Gain/M-param\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"FTM\", \"pi0\", \"4K\", 14.7, 3675.0]\n          - [\"Universal LoRA (r16)\", \"pi0\", \"2.0M\", 11.2, 5.60]\n          - [\"Meta-Brain\", \"pi0\", \"6.1M\", 24.8, 4.07]\n          - [\"Meta-Brain + CM\", \"pi0\", \"6.1M\", 27.2, 4.46]\n          - [\"VLA-GSE*\", \"Qwen3-VL-4B\", \"114M\", 27.6, 0.24]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot (Figure 5 in paper): x-axis = trainable params (log scale, 1K to 200M), y-axis = gain over frozen baseline (%). Points: FTM (bottom-left, high slope from origin), Universal LoRA (mid-left), Meta-Brain (mid, star marker), Meta-Brain+CM (mid, diamond), VLA-GSE (far right, asterisk with cross-backbone caveat). Pareto front line through FTM→Meta-Brain→VLA-GSE. Meta-Brain clearly on or near Pareto front. Dashed iso-efficiency lines (constant gain/M) for reference.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scatter plot 是 Claim 3 的视觉锚点。关键信息：在 log-scale x 轴上，\n      Meta-Brain 距 VLA-GSE 向左一个数量级以上，但 y 轴差距很小（24.8 vs 27.6）。\n      论文应在图注中明确 VLA-GSE 使用不同 backbone（Qwen3-VL-4B），\n      并引导读者关注 gain-over-own-baseline 指标而非绝对值。\n      Universal LoRA 的数据点是重要的 in-backbone 参照——它证明仅增加参数（从 2M 到 6M）\n      不如增加路由（从 universal 到 routed），因为 rank-48 universal LoRA 预期仍 ~67%。\n\n  - name: \"Correction Memory ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      Compare Meta-Brain with and without Correction Memory. CM modulates routing \n      weights via retrieved exemplars. Quantify marginal gain.\n    expected_results:\n      meta_brain_no_cm: 78.4\n      meta_brain_with_cm: 80.8\n      cm_ablation_delta: 2.4\n      cm_delta_camera: 2.0\n      cm_delta_light: 2.0\n      cm_delta_background: 2.0\n      cm_delta_noise: 4.0\n      cm_delta_layout: 2.0\n      cm_delta_robot: 3.0\n      cm_alpha_learned: 0.18\n      cm_retrieval_latency_ms: 0.8\n      cm_faiss_index_size_MB: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      CM 的 2.4% 增益来自两个机制：\n      (1) 路由权重精修：对于 PAR 不确定的样本（routing entropy 较高），\n      CM 从 FAISS 检索到的 k-NN exemplar 提供了基于历史成功案例的权重校准，\n      将这些 borderline 样本推向正确专家。noise 类型获益最大（+4.0%），\n      因为 sensor_noise 与 camera 扰动在激活空间中距离较近，PAR 在此区域\n      routing 不确定性最高，CM 的 exemplar matching 恰好能消除这一歧义。\n      (2) 校正强度调制：learned alpha=0.18 说明 CM 的权重修正幅度温和，\n      不会覆盖 PAR 的主信号，仅在需要时提供微调——这是「optional module」\n      定位的实验支撑。\n      CM 只增加 1 个可学习参数（alpha）+ CPU-bound FAISS 检索（0.8ms），\n      对推理延迟几乎无影响，使其成为一个低风险的即插即用模块。\n      2.4% gain 在 [1, 4] 范围内，足以在论文中报告但不构成核心贡献——\n      这恰好是理想定位：CM 是额外加分项而非系统必要组件。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"CM ablation per-perturbation\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"w/o CM\", \"w/ CM\", \"CM Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 72.0, 74.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"light\", 78.0, 80.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"background\", 76.0, 78.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"noise\", 70.0, 74.0, \"+4.0\"]\n          - [\"layout\", 88.0, 90.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"robot\", 86.0, 89.0, \"+3.0\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 78.4, 80.8, \"+2.4\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: w/ and w/o CM for each perturbation type. CM gains highlighted with delta annotations. Noise and robot types show largest improvements.\"\n      - \"Scatter: per-sample routing entropy (x) vs CM-induced weight change magnitude (y), showing CM intervenes most on high-entropy (uncertain) samples.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CM 对 reviewer concern C6 的回应很清晰：2.4% gain with 1 learned param, \n      0.8ms latency, 完全 optional。建议在论文中将 CM 放在 ablation section 而非 \n      main method，避免给审稿人造成「系统过于复杂」的印象。\n      noise 类型的 +4% 增益可以作为 case study 展示 CM 的工作机制。\n\n  - name: \"Router architecture comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      Compare PAR router variants: 2-layer MLP, linear classifier, attention-based. \n      All on PaliGemma layer 6. Measure routing accuracy and downstream success.\n    expected_results:\n      mlp_routing_acc: 97.2\n      mlp_downstream: 78.4\n      mlp_params_K: 48\n      linear_routing_acc: 94.1\n      linear_downstream: 76.6\n      linear_params_K: 6\n      attention_routing_acc: 97.8\n      attention_downstream: 78.8\n      attention_params_K: 196\n      mlp_vs_linear_downstream_gap: 1.8\n      mlp_vs_attention_downstream_gap: -0.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      三种路由器的性能梯度与 Phase 0 的分类难度分析一致：\n      (1) Linear (94.1% → 76.6%): 线性可分性已经很强（Phase 0 证实 layer 6 的类别边界\n      几乎线性），但 ~6% 的误差集中在 Visual 子类型间的边界区域（noise vs camera），\n      导致下游 1.8% 的性能损失。线性模型只有 6K params，极其轻量。\n      (2) MLP (97.2% → 78.4%): 两层 MLP 捕捉到非线性边界，将路由误差压缩到 2.8%，\n      在参数效率（48K）和性能间取得最佳平衡。48K 相对于 6M LoRA params 可忽略不计。\n      (3) Attention (97.8% → 78.8%): attention 机制可以利用 token 间关系进行路由，\n      略优于 MLP (+0.6% routing, +0.4% downstream)，但参数量增加 4x（196K），\n      增益不具统计显著性。\n      MLP 是论文默认选择的合理性得到验证：比 linear 明显好、与 attention 实质等价、\n      参数最经济。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Router architecture comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Router\", \"Params\", \"Routing Acc (%)\", \"Downstream (%)\", \"Δ vs MLP\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Linear\", \"6K\", 94.1, 76.6, \"-1.8\"]\n          - [\"2-layer MLP (default)\", \"48K\", 97.2, 78.4, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Attention-based\", \"196K\", 97.8, 78.8, \"+0.4\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Small dual-axis bar chart: routing accuracy (left axis) and downstream success (right axis) for 3 router types. Shows diminishing returns beyond MLP.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这个实验回答了一个隐含问题：路由器复杂度如何影响整体系统？\n      答案是：影响极小。94.1→97.2% 的路由精度提升带来 1.8% 下游增益，\n      但 97.2→97.8% 的进一步提升仅带来 0.4%。这是因为 Phase 0 分类本身很容易，\n      简单模型已足够——与 reviewer concern C1 的回应一致。\n      建议在 appendix 报告此结果，主文只提 MLP 作为默认配置。\n\n  - name: \"6-class vs 3-class routing comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      Compare 6-class fine-grained routing (6 LoRA experts) vs 3-class coarse routing \n      (3 experts). Test whether finer granularity justifies additional parameters.\n    expected_results:\n      three_class_overall: 78.4\n      three_class_params_M: 6.1\n      six_class_overall: 79.4\n      six_class_params_M: 12.2\n      marginal_gain: 1.0\n      marginal_gain_per_additional_expert: 0.33\n      six_class_camera: 74.0\n      six_class_light: 80.0\n      six_class_background: 78.0\n      six_class_noise: 74.0\n      six_class_layout: 88.0\n      six_class_robot: 82.0\n      six_class_routing_acc: 96.8\n      intra_visual_gain: 1.5\n      spatial_physical_gain: -0.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      6-class routing 仅带来 1.0% 的边际增益，原因：\n      (1) Phase 0 已显示 intra-Visual 子类型之间的特征距离远小于 inter-category 距离，\n      6-class 在 Visual 子类型间的路由精度（96.8%）略低于 3-class（97.2%），\n      说明更细的边界带来了更多的路由噪声；\n      (2) Visual 子类型的校正模式确实有差异（camera 需要修复 color/geometry 畸变，\n      noise 需要去噪平滑），所以 6 个专家在 Visual 上略优 (+1.5%)，\n      但这一增益被 spatial/physical 的轻微退化 (-0.7%) 部分抵消——\n      6-class 中 layout 和 robot 各自只有一个专家（与 3-class 相同），\n      但 router 增加了 4 个 Visual 类别输出后 softmax 分母增大，\n      导致 layout/robot 的 routing confidence 略降；\n      (3) 6 个 LoRA 专家的参数量翻倍（12.2M），但增益仅 1.0%，\n      gain/additional-param 极低（0.33%/expert vs 3-class 的 4.07 gain/M）。\n      结论：3-class taxonomy 在效率-性能 trade-off 上是最优粒度，\n      与 Phase 0 的 mechanistic 分析（early/mid/late layers 对应 Visual/Spatial/Physical）一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"6-class vs 3-class per-perturbation\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"3-class\", \"6-class\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 72.0, 74.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"light\", 78.0, 80.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"background\", 76.0, 78.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"noise\", 70.0, 74.0, \"+4.0\"]\n          - [\"layout\", 88.0, 88.0, \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"robot\", 86.0, 82.0, \"-4.0\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 78.4, 79.4, \"+1.0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 3-class vs 6-class per type. Visual types show small gains; robot shows slight regression. Annotations: total param cost for each configuration.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这个结果直接回应 reviewer concern C5（3-class 是否太粗）：\n      答案是「对当前任务集合，3-class 是 sweet spot」。论文应在 discussion 中 \n      承认 6-class 在某些 Visual 子类型上有额外区分度，但将 3-class 定位为 \n      Occam's razor 选择。robot 类的 -4% 退化值得关注——可能是因为 6 个 softmax \n      输出中 robot 的 prior probability 被稀释。如果 LIBERO-Plus 扩展更多物理扰动\n      子类型，6-class 或更细的 taxonomy 可能变得必要。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-backbone validation — OpenVLA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      Replicate Phase 0 + Phase 1 core pipeline on OpenVLA to test generalizability \n      of perturbation-diagnostic routing across architectures.\n    expected_results:\n      cross_backbone: \"OpenVLA (SigLIP + Llama-2-7B)\"\n      phase0_3class_f1: 0.972\n      phase0_best_layer: 8\n      phase0_pooling: \"mean\"\n      openvla_frozen_overall: 48.2\n      openvla_universal_lora_overall: 58.6\n      openvla_meta_brain_overall: 70.4\n      openvla_gain_over_frozen: 22.2\n      openvla_gain_over_universal: 11.8\n      openvla_oracle_overall: 71.8\n      openvla_oracle_par_gap: 1.4\n      openvla_routing_diagonality: 0.89\n    result_rationale: >\n      OpenVLA 上的复现确认 perturbation-diagnostic routing 是跨架构通用的：\n      (1) Phase 0 F1=0.972（略低于 pi0 的 0.993）：OpenVLA 使用 SigLIP（非 PaliGemma）\n      作为视觉编码器，最佳层从 layer 6 移至 layer 8，但分类精度依然极高。\n      这与 SAFE 论文在 OpenVLA 上的 probing 结果一致，进一步支持「VLA 内部表征 \n      普遍编码扰动类型信息」的核心假说。\n      (2) gain over frozen = 22.2%（pi0 上为 24.8%）：绝对增益略低，因为 OpenVLA \n      的 frozen baseline 更低（48.2% vs 53.6%），说明 OpenVLA 本身对扰动更脆弱，\n      校正难度更大。但 gain 仍在 best-tier 范围 [22, 28] 的低端。\n      (3) gain over universal = 11.8%（pi0 上为 13.6%）：路由增益在 OpenVLA 上 \n      同样显著，确认了 Claim 2 的跨架构有效性。\n      (4) Oracle-PAR gap = 1.4%（pi0 上为 1.2%）：略大但仍在 [0, 2] 内，\n      与 Phase 0 F1 略低（0.972 vs 0.993）一致。\n      OpenVLA 的较低绝对性能可归因于其较小的视觉编码器容量和不同的训练数据分布。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-backbone comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"pi0 (PaliGemma)\", \"OpenVLA (SigLIP)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Phase 0 3-class F1\", 0.993, 0.972]\n          - [\"Best probe layer\", 6, 8]\n          - [\"Frozen baseline (%)\", 53.6, 48.2]\n          - [\"Universal LoRA (%)\", 64.8, 58.6]\n          - [\"Meta-Brain (%)\", 78.4, 70.4]\n          - [\"Oracle (%)\", 79.6, 71.8]\n          - [\"Gain over frozen\", 24.8, 22.2]\n          - [\"Gain over universal\", 13.6, 11.8]\n          - [\"Oracle-PAR gap\", 1.2, 1.4]\n          - [\"Routing diagonality\", 0.92, 0.89]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side ablation ladder bars for pi0 and OpenVLA, showing parallel staircase pattern despite different absolute values. Gain-over-frozen annotations highlight comparable relative improvements.\"\n    analysis: >\n      跨 backbone 验证是应对 reviewer concern C3 的关键实验。\n      尽管绝对数值不同（OpenVLA 整体低 ~8%），增益模式高度一致：\n      universal→meta-brain 的 gain 在两个 backbone 上分别为 13.6% 和 11.8%，\n      routing diagonality 分别为 0.92 和 0.89——都远高于 random baseline (0.33)。\n      Phase 0 的最佳层从 layer 6 (PaliGemma) 移至 layer 8 (SigLIP) 符合预期：\n      不同视觉编码器的信息编码深度不同，但扰动类型信息的可提取性是通用的。\n      论文中应以 gain-over-baseline 为主要比较指标，避免直接对比绝对值。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA layer placement ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      Vary which PaliGemma layers receive LoRA. Test whether optimal layer placement \n      differs by perturbation type (early for Visual, mid for Spatial, late for Physical).\n    expected_results:\n      lora_v_early_2_8: 77.2\n      lora_v_mid_6_12: 72.8\n      lora_v_late_12_18: 68.4\n      lora_v_all: 76.0\n      lora_s_early_2_8: 82.0\n      lora_s_mid_6_12: 91.4\n      lora_s_late_12_18: 86.0\n      lora_s_all: 90.0\n      lora_p_early_2_8: 78.0\n      lora_p_mid_6_12: 82.0\n      lora_p_late_12_18: 89.2\n      lora_p_all: 88.0\n      optimal_v: \"early (layers 2-8)\"\n      optimal_s: \"mid (layers 6-12)\"\n      optimal_p: \"late (layers 12-18)\"\n      type_aligned_overall: 80.2\n      all_layers_overall: 78.4\n      type_aligned_gain_over_all_layers: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      层放置的最优分布与 VLA 处理扰动的 mechanistic 假设高度吻合：\n      (1) LoRA-V 最优在 early layers (2-8): Visual 扰动（camera/light/background/noise）\n      在视觉编码阶段损坏表征，early layers 是信号最先被破坏的地方，\n      在此处施加 LoRA 校正效率最高。LoRA-V 在 late layers 仅 68.4%（接近 universal LoRA），\n      因为视觉损坏在传播到高层后已经耦合到语义表征中，难以局部修复。\n      (2) LoRA-S 最优在 mid layers (6-12): Spatial 扰动改变物体空间关系，\n      这类信息在 mid layers 被编码为 spatial token relationships。\n      LoRA-S 在 mid layers 达 91.4%（超过 all-layers 的 90.0%），\n      说明集中校正比分散校正更有效——避免了 early/late layers 的无用更新。\n      (3) LoRA-P 最优在 late layers (12-18): Physical 扰动影响动力学属性，\n      这些信息在高层被整合为 action planning 信号。LoRA-P 在 late layers 达 89.2%。\n      Type-aligned 配置（每个专家放在最优层区间）比 all-layers 配置高 1.8%，\n      同时每个专家的参数量减少 ~60%（仅覆盖 6 层而非 18 层）。\n      这为更极致的参数效率提供了方向，但增加了系统复杂度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Layer placement × expert type (own-type success rate %)\"\n        columns: [\"Expert\", \"Early (2-8)\", \"Mid (6-12)\", \"Late (12-18)\", \"All layers\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA-V (Visual)\", 77.2, 72.8, 68.4, 76.0]\n          - [\"LoRA-S (Spatial)\", 82.0, 91.4, 86.0, 90.0]\n          - [\"LoRA-P (Physical)\", 78.0, 82.0, 89.2, 88.0]\n      - name: \"System-level layer placement comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Configuration\", \"Params/expert\", \"Visual\", \"Spatial\", \"Physical\", \"Overall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All layers (default)\", \"~2.0M\", 76.0, 90.0, 88.0, 78.4]\n          - [\"Type-aligned layers\", \"~0.8M\", 77.2, 91.4, 89.2, 80.2]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3×3 heatmap: expert rows × layer-group columns, cell values = own-type success rate. Clear diagonal pattern (V-early, S-mid, P-late) with highest values along the diagonal.\"\n    analysis: >\n      层放置 ablation 提供了 mechanistic insight 而非直接的系统设计改进。\n      对角模式（V-early, S-mid, P-late）与 VLA 的分层信息处理模型一致，\n      为 Phase 0 的单层分类结果提供了因果方向的支持：layer 6 能区分扰动类型，\n      因为不同类型的信息损坏恰好在该层汇聚/分离。\n      Type-aligned 配置带来 1.8% 增益和 60% 参数节省，但增加了工程复杂度\n      （需要为每个专家配置不同的层 mask）。建议在论文 appendix 中作为 \n      「进一步优化方向」报告，主系统保持 all-layers 的简洁配置。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11192,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11192},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40703030-3e58-41b3-9b6d-2da547bf07b9","uuid":"ebb1e0ba-9200-434d-a38e-bb3a8907d26c"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":440556,"duration_api_ms":441654,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Original framing holds as-is. Headline: Meta-Brain achieves 78.4% on LIBERO-Plus \n  with 6M params (80.8% with CM), closing 90% of the gap to VLA-GSE (81.2%, 114M params) \n  at 19x fewer trainable parameters. All three claims land cleanly — Phase 0 diagnosability \n  enables zero-overhead routing (Claim 1), the ablation ladder shows targeted > uniform \n  correction with 13.6% gain over universal LoRA (Claim 2), and the parameter efficiency \n  scatter plot positions Meta-Brain at 4.13 gain/M-param vs VLA-GSE's 0.24 (Claim 3). \n  Specialization is validated by 20% max delta (camera type) and strong cross-type \n  degradation of mismatched experts. Oracle-PAR gap of 1.2% confirms Phase 0 signal is \n  actionable. Paper should lead with the ablation ladder figure and close with the \n  parameter-efficiency scatter plot.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"LoRA expert training — 3 specialized + 1 universal\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      Train 4 LoRA adapters (rank 16) on frozen pi0 PaliGemma layers: LoRA-V (Visual), \n      LoRA-S (Spatial), LoRA-P (Physical), Universal LoRA (mixed). Evaluate each on \n      own-type and cross-type perturbations.\n    expected_results:\n      lora_v_visual_avg: 76.0\n      lora_v_camera: 74.0\n      lora_v_light: 80.0\n      lora_v_background: 78.0\n      lora_v_noise: 72.0\n      lora_v_on_spatial: 60.0\n      lora_v_on_physical: 54.0\n      lora_s_layout: 90.0\n      lora_s_on_visual_avg: 46.5\n      lora_s_on_physical: 56.0\n      lora_p_robot: 88.0\n      lora_p_on_visual_avg: 44.0\n      lora_p_on_spatial: 62.0\n      universal_lora_overall: 64.8\n      universal_camera: 54.0\n      universal_light: 66.0\n      universal_background: 62.0\n      universal_noise: 54.0\n      universal_layout: 78.0\n      universal_robot: 74.0\n      per_type_specialization_delta_max: 20.0\n      per_type_specialization_delta_min: 12.0\n      cross_type_degradation_max: -20.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Rank-16 LoRA on PaliGemma layers provides足够的修正容量处理单一扰动类型。\n      专用 LoRA 在其目标类型上大幅超越 universal LoRA（最大 delta=20%，camera 类型），因为：\n      (1) Visual 扰动主要破坏 PaliGemma 早期视觉编码，LoRA-V 的全部容量用于修复这一信号通路，\n      而 universal LoRA 必须将同样容量分摊到三类截然不同的校正模式上；\n      (2) Spatial (layout) 扰动修改物体空间关系，LoRA-S 学到的校正向量直接对齐中层空间表征，\n      在 layout 上达 90%——这是所有组合中最高的，因为 layout 是单一子类、分布集中；\n      (3) Physical (robot) 扰动改变力学属性，LoRA-P 在 robot 上达 88%。\n      Cross-type 严重退化（LoRA-V 在 physical 仅 54%，低于 frozen baseline 的 56%）证实\n      三类扰动所需的校正模式确实互不兼容——这是 Claim 2 的关键论据：专用路由并非锦上添花，\n      而是必要条件。Universal LoRA 在 64.8% 饱和，因为 rank-16 的有限容量在三类矛盾梯度\n      方向间折衷，导致每种类型都欠校正。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Expert cross-evaluation matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Expert\", \"camera\", \"light\", \"background\", \"noise\", \"layout\", \"robot\", \"Overall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA-V\", 74.0, 80.0, 78.0, 72.0, 60.0, 54.0, 69.7]\n          - [\"LoRA-S\", 44.0, 52.0, 48.0, 42.0, 90.0, 56.0, 55.3]\n          - [\"LoRA-P\", 40.0, 50.0, 46.0, 40.0, 62.0, 88.0, 54.3]\n          - [\"Universal\", 54.0, 66.0, 62.0, 54.0, 78.0, 74.0, 64.8]\n          - [\"Frozen pi0\", 42.0, 58.0, 52.0, 46.0, 68.0, 56.0, 53.6]\n      - name: \"Specialization delta (own-type expert minus universal)\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation type\", \"Specialist\", \"Universal\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 74.0, 54.0, \"+20.0\"]\n          - [\"light\", 80.0, 66.0, \"+14.0\"]\n          - [\"background\", 78.0, 62.0, \"+16.0\"]\n          - [\"noise\", 72.0, 54.0, \"+18.0\"]\n          - [\"layout\", 90.0, 78.0, \"+12.0\"]\n          - [\"robot\", 88.0, 74.0, \"+14.0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×6 cross-evaluation matrix (expert rows × perturbation columns), strong diagonal blocks visible — LoRA-V hot on left 4 columns, LoRA-S hot on layout, LoRA-P hot on robot. Off-diagonal cells cool/cold, many below frozen baseline.\"\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: per-type success rate for each expert + universal + frozen, clearly showing each specialist dominates its own types while failing on others.\"\n    analysis: >\n      最核心发现：cross-type 退化的幅度（最大 -20% vs frozen）与 own-type 提升幅度（最大 +20%）\n      几乎对称，说明 LoRA 学到的不是通用「鲁棒性」而是类型特异的校正映射。\n      Universal LoRA 在每个类型上都不如对应专家，差距最大的是 camera（-20）和 noise（-18），\n      最小的是 layout（-12）。Layout 差距最小因为它是 Spatial 类的唯一子类型，universal LoRA \n      分配给 spatial 校正的有效容量比例相对较高。这为 Meta-Brain 的路由设计提供了直接动机：\n      如果能正确识别扰动类型并激活对应专家，就能同时获得所有类型上的最优校正。\n\n  - name: \"Meta-Brain assembly — PAR + LoRA bank E2E\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      Assemble PAR router (PaliGemma layer 6 MLP) + 3 frozen LoRA experts with soft routing. \n      Fine-tune only PAR routing weights end-to-end on LIBERO-Plus rollouts.\n    expected_results:\n      libero_plus_overall: 78.4\n      camera: 72.0\n      light: 78.0\n      background: 76.0\n      noise: 70.0\n      layout: 88.0\n      robot: 86.0\n      visual_avg: 74.0\n      spatial_avg: 88.0\n      physical_avg: 86.0\n      routing_diagonality: 0.92\n      par_visual_weight_on_lora_v: 0.91\n      par_spatial_weight_on_lora_s: 0.93\n      par_physical_weight_on_lora_p: 0.92\n      trainable_params_M: 6.1\n      routing_params_K: 48\n      gain_over_frozen: 24.8\n      gain_over_universal_lora: 13.6\n    result_rationale: >\n      PAR router 利用 Phase 0 已验证的 layer 6 激活信号（F1=0.993）进行软路由，\n      routing diagonality 达到 0.92 意味着 92% 的权重正确分配给目标专家。\n      剩余 8% 的\"泄漏\"实际上是有益的：\n      (1) 部分扰动（如 background clutter + 轻微 layout shift 同时出现）需要混合校正；\n      (2) soft routing 的平滑梯度使得 PAR 在 E2E fine-tuning 中可以学到比 hard routing \n      更精细的权重配置。\n      整体 78.4% 低于各专家在 own-type 上的最优成绩的加权平均（~81%），差距来源：\n      (a) 8% 路由泄漏导致部分样本获得次优校正；\n      (b) PAR fine-tuning 只调路由权重、冻结 LoRA，整体达不到联合训练的上界。\n      但 78.4% 已经比 universal LoRA 高 13.6%，证明路由带来的专家选择增益远超路由误差成本。\n      layout 和 robot 达到 88% 和 86%（接近 oracle 的 plan_002 数据），因为这两类是 \n      单一子类型、PAR 分类难度最低。Visual 子类型（camera 72%、noise 70%）相对低一些，\n      因为 4 种视觉扰动之间存在一定混淆（noise vs camera 的 PAR 权重偶尔偏移）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Meta-Brain per-perturbation breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"Frozen\", \"Universal\", \"Meta-Brain\", \"Gain vs Frozen\", \"Gain vs Universal\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 42.0, 54.0, 72.0, \"+30.0\", \"+18.0\"]\n          - [\"light\", 58.0, 66.0, 78.0, \"+20.0\", \"+12.0\"]\n          - [\"background\", 52.0, 62.0, 76.0, \"+24.0\", \"+14.0\"]\n          - [\"noise\", 46.0, 54.0, 70.0, \"+24.0\", \"+16.0\"]\n          - [\"layout\", 68.0, 78.0, 88.0, \"+20.0\", \"+10.0\"]\n          - [\"robot\", 56.0, 74.0, 86.0, \"+30.0\", \"+12.0\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 53.6, 64.8, 78.4, \"+24.8\", \"+13.6\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Architecture diagram: Frozen pi0 → PaliGemma layer 6 → PAR MLP → [p_V, p_S, p_P] soft weights → LoRA-V/S/P bank → h_corrected = h_frozen + Σ p_k·LoRA_k(h). Only PAR weights are trainable (48K params), LoRA experts frozen from plan_002.\"\n      - \"Routing weight heatmap: 3×3 matrix (perturbation category × expert), near-diagonal with 0.91-0.93 on diagonal, 0.03-0.05 off-diagonal. Color-coded to show PAR correctly identifies perturbation type.\"\n      - \"Per-perturbation grouped bar chart: 6 clusters (one per type), 3 bars each (frozen/universal/meta-brain), showing consistent improvement across all types.\"\n    analysis: >\n      13.6% gain over universal LoRA 是 Claim 2 的核心数值。在参数量相同（6M = 3×2M \n      vs 1×2M + 相同总 rank budget 的另一种分配）甚至 Meta-Brain 用了 3 倍参数的情况下，\n      关键洞察不是「更多参数 = 更好」而是「路由后的容量利用率远高于混合训练」。\n      可做公平对比：rank-48 universal LoRA（与 3×rank-16 参数量相当）预期仍然饱和在 ~67%，\n      因为高 rank 并不能解决梯度冲突——这是 plan_005 ablation ladder 要验证的。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle routing ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      Replace PAR with ground-truth perturbation labels for hard routing. \n      Measures upper bound for routing quality.\n    expected_results:\n      oracle_overall: 79.6\n      oracle_camera: 74.0\n      oracle_light: 78.0\n      oracle_background: 78.0\n      oracle_noise: 72.0\n      oracle_layout: 88.0\n      oracle_robot: 88.0\n      oracle_par_gap: 1.2\n      oracle_par_gap_camera: 2.0\n      oracle_par_gap_light: 0.0\n      oracle_par_gap_background: 2.0\n      oracle_par_gap_noise: 2.0\n      oracle_par_gap_layout: 0.0\n      oracle_par_gap_robot: 2.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Oracle-PAR gap 仅 1.2%，直接证明 Phase 0 的分类信号在下游任务中是 actionable 的。\n      Gap 主要来自 Visual 子类型（camera +2, background +2, noise +2），因为 PAR 在 \n      4 种 Visual 子类型间存在少量混淆（~8% 路由泄漏），导致部分 Visual 样本获得了 \n      LoRA-S/P 的轻微干扰。Layout 和 robot 的 gap 为 0-2%，因为这两类在 Phase 0 \n      的分类准确率接近 100%（单一子类型、特征空间高度分离）。\n      1.2% gap 远小于 Meta-Brain vs Universal LoRA 的 13.6% gain，这意味着即使路由 \n      有少量误差，路由策略本身的收益也远大于误差带来的损失。\n      Oracle 79.6% 低于各专家 own-type 最优的简单加权平均（~81%），因为 oracle routing \n      是 hard routing（1-hot 权重），丢失了 soft routing 在某些混合扰动样本上的 \n      blending 优势。这也解释了为什么 PAR 的 soft routing 在某些类型上能接近 oracle。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Oracle vs PAR per-perturbation gap\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"PAR\", \"Oracle\", \"Gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 72.0, 74.0, 2.0]\n          - [\"light\", 78.0, 78.0, 0.0]\n          - [\"background\", 76.0, 78.0, 2.0]\n          - [\"noise\", 70.0, 72.0, 2.0]\n          - [\"layout\", 88.0, 88.0, 0.0]\n          - [\"robot\", 86.0, 88.0, 2.0]\n          - [\"Overall\", 78.4, 79.6, 1.2]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: PAR vs Oracle per perturbation type, gap annotations on top. Visual types show small consistent gaps; Spatial/Physical nearly identical.\"\n    analysis: >\n      1.2% gap 是对 reviewer concern C1（「Phase 0 分类太简单，路由无用」）的最佳回应：\n      分类简单 ≠ 路由无价值。分类简单意味着路由几乎免费获得正确性（zero overhead），\n      而 13.6% 的 gain over universal 证明路由的价值在于下游校正，不在路由本身的难度。\n      Oracle gap 小反而是优势——说明 PAR 已经接近天花板，无需更复杂的路由器。\n\n  - name: \"Ablation ladder — Frozen → Universal → Meta-Brain → Oracle\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic comparison on LIBERO-Plus with 5 seeds. Core evidence for Claim 2.\n    expected_results:\n      frozen_mean: 53.6\n      frozen_std: 1.4\n      universal_mean: 64.8\n      universal_std: 1.8\n      meta_brain_mean: 78.4\n      meta_brain_std: 1.6\n      oracle_mean: 79.6\n      oracle_std: 1.2\n      gain_frozen_to_universal: 11.2\n      gain_universal_to_meta_brain: 13.6\n      gain_meta_brain_to_oracle: 1.2\n      gain_frozen_to_meta_brain: 24.8\n      p_value_universal_vs_meta_brain: 0.0003\n      p_value_meta_brain_vs_oracle: 0.14\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-seed 统计验证下，ablation ladder 呈现清晰的三级阶梯：\n      (1) Frozen→Universal (+11.2%): universal LoRA 提供了基础的扰动鲁棒性，\n      证明 PaliGemma 层的 LoRA adaptation 是有效的校正机制。标准差 1.8% 较高，\n      因为 universal LoRA 在不同 seed 下对不同扰动类型的容量分配方式不稳定（\n      有时偏重 visual、有时偏重 spatial），导致 run-to-run 方差较大。\n      (2) Universal→Meta-Brain (+13.6%, p<0.001): 路由带来的增益甚至超过 universal LoRA \n      自身 over frozen 的增益，统计显著。这是 Claim 2 最强的证据——同样的 LoRA capacity，\n      路由后的利用效率比混合使用高出一倍以上。Meta-Brain 的标准差 1.6% 低于 universal \n      的 1.8%，因为路由机制减少了容量分配的随机性。\n      (3) Meta-Brain→Oracle (+1.2%, p=0.14): 差异不显著，证明 PAR 路由已接近上界。\n      这一不显著结果本身就是积极信号——说明无需 oracle 标签，Phase 0 分类足矣。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Ablation ladder summary (5 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Params\", \"Overall ± std\", \"Gain over Frozen\", \"Gain over Prev. Step\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Frozen pi0\", \"0\", \"53.6 ± 1.4\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Universal LoRA (r16)\", \"~2M\", \"64.8 ± 1.8\", \"+11.2\", \"+11.2\"]\n          - [\"Meta-Brain (PAR+ALB)\", \"~6M\", \"78.4 ± 1.6\", \"+24.8\", \"+13.6\"]\n          - [\"Oracle routing\", \"~6M\", \"79.6 ± 1.2\", \"+26.0\", \"+1.2\"]\n      - name: \"Per-perturbation ablation (mean over 5 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"Frozen\", \"Universal\", \"Meta-Brain\", \"Oracle\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 42.0, 54.0, 72.0, 74.0]\n          - [\"light\", 58.0, 66.0, 78.0, 78.0]\n          - [\"background\", 52.0, 62.0, 76.0, 78.0]\n          - [\"noise\", 46.0, 54.0, 70.0, 72.0]\n          - [\"layout\", 68.0, 78.0, 88.0, 88.0]\n          - [\"robot\", 56.0, 74.0, 86.0, 88.0]\n          - [\"Overall\", 53.6, 64.8, 78.4, 79.6]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart (Figure 4 in paper): 4 bars per perturbation type + overall, ascending Frozen→Universal→Meta-Brain→Oracle. Error bars from 5 seeds. Clear staircase pattern; biggest jump is Universal→Meta-Brain.\"\n      - \"Delta decomposition stacked bar: overall gain 26.0% (oracle over frozen) decomposed into universal contribution (11.2), routing contribution (13.6), routing-perfection headroom (1.2).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Ablation ladder 的核心叙事：从 frozen 到 oracle 的 26.0% 总增益中，\n      routing 贡献了 13.6%（52%），universal adaptation 贡献了 11.2%（43%），\n      routing 精度 headroom 仅 1.2%（5%）。这意味着 perturbation-diagnostic routing \n      不是边际优化，而是与 LoRA adaptation 本身同等量级的增益来源。\n      统计显著性分析确认 universal→meta-brain 的增益是 robust 的（p<0.001），\n      而 meta-brain→oracle 的差异不显著（p=0.14），为 PAR 路由的实用性提供了严格支持。\n\n  - name: \"FTM/FLA reproduction on pi0\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      Reproduce FTM on pi0 for visual perturbations. Compare with Meta-Brain on visual \n      and demonstrate Meta-Brain's advantage on non-visual types.\n    expected_results:\n      ftm_camera: 70.0\n      ftm_light: 76.0\n      ftm_background: 72.0\n      ftm_noise: 68.0\n      ftm_visual_avg: 71.5\n      ftm_layout: 68.0\n      ftm_robot: 56.0\n      ftm_overall: 68.3\n      ftm_params_K: 4\n      meta_brain_visual_avg: 74.0\n      meta_brain_advantage_visual: 2.5\n      meta_brain_advantage_overall: 10.1\n      meta_brain_advantage_non_visual: 22.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      FTM 在 pi0 上的复现结果合理偏低于原论文（原论文用不同 backbone 且只报告视觉扰动）。\n      FTM 在 visual 子类型上达 71.5%（接近 LoRA-V 的 76.0%），说明 FTM 的 feature \n      modulation 策略确实能有效修复视觉损坏——这与 FTM 原论文的结论一致。\n      但 FTM 在 layout (68.0%) 和 robot (56.0%) 上几乎无增益或低于 universal LoRA，\n      因为 FTM 的设计假设扰动仅存在于视觉通道，其 modulation 无法处理空间关系和物理属性的变化。\n      Meta-Brain 在 visual 上略优于 FTM (+2.5%)，因为 LoRA-V 有更多参数（2M vs 4K）\n      可以学到更精细的校正。关键差异在非 visual 类型：Meta-Brain 在 layout+robot 上\n      平均 87.0% vs FTM 的 62.0%（+25.0%），这 25% 的差距直接论证了多类型校正的必要性。\n      FTM 的 4K 参数量在 per-param visual gain 上极其高效，但 scope-limited——\n      这在 parameter efficiency scatter plot (plan_007) 中会成为一个有趣的数据点。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"FTM vs Meta-Brain comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"FTM (4K)\", \"Meta-Brain (6M)\", \"LoRA-V (2M)\", \"Universal (2M)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 70.0, 72.0, 74.0, 54.0]\n          - [\"light\", 76.0, 78.0, 80.0, 66.0]\n          - [\"background\", 72.0, 76.0, 78.0, 62.0]\n          - [\"noise\", 68.0, 70.0, 72.0, 54.0]\n          - [\"layout\", 68.0, 88.0, 60.0, 78.0]\n          - [\"robot\", 56.0, 86.0, 54.0, 74.0]\n          - [\"Overall\", 68.3, 78.4, 69.7, 64.8]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart: 6 axes (perturbation types), overlaid polygons for FTM/Meta-Brain/Universal. FTM polygon inflated in left 4 axes (visual) but deflated in right 2 (spatial/physical); Meta-Brain polygon uniformly large.\"\n    analysis: >\n      FTM 是一个重要的 baseline，因为它代表了「单模态专家」的最佳案例。\n      Meta-Brain 的价值主张不是在任何单一类型上打败 FTM，而是在所有类型上同时提供 \n      强大校正——这正是 perturbation-diagnostic routing 的设计目标。\n      在论文中应将 FTM 定位为「visual-only routing 的上界参考」，\n      并强调 Meta-Brain 的 multi-type coverage 是其独特贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Parameter efficiency analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      Compute gain-over-frozen per method, normalize by trainable params. \n      Generate scatter plot (x=params, y=gain). Core visual evidence for Claim 3.\n    expected_results:\n      meta_brain_gain: 24.8\n      meta_brain_params_M: 6.1\n      meta_brain_gain_per_M: 4.07\n      meta_brain_with_cm_gain: 27.2\n      meta_brain_with_cm_params_M: 6.1\n      meta_brain_with_cm_gain_per_M: 4.46\n      universal_lora_gain: 11.2\n      universal_lora_params_M: 2.0\n      universal_lora_gain_per_M: 5.60\n      ftm_gain_overall: 14.7\n      ftm_params_M: 0.004\n      ftm_gain_per_M: 3675.0\n      vla_gse_gain: 27.6\n      vla_gse_params_M: 114.0\n      vla_gse_gain_per_M: 0.24\n      meta_brain_vs_vla_gse_param_ratio: 18.7\n      meta_brain_vs_vla_gse_gain_ratio: 0.90\n      meta_brain_pareto_optimal: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Meta-Brain 的 gain/M-param = 4.07，是 VLA-GSE (0.24) 的 17 倍。\n      在 scatter plot 上 Meta-Brain 位于 Pareto 前沿的关键位置：\n      (1) 相比 VLA-GSE：以 5.3% 的参数量达到 90% 的 gain，参数效率高 17x；\n      (2) 相比 Universal LoRA：gain/M 虽低（4.07 vs 5.60），但绝对 gain 高 13.6%，\n      说明 3x 参数扩展用于路由（而非增大 rank）是高效的；\n      (3) 相比 FTM：FTM 的 per-param efficiency 极高（3675 gain/M）但绝对 gain \n      受限于 visual-only scope，在 scatter plot 上位于右下角「高效率低总量」区域。\n      这三对比较构成 Claim 3 的完整论证：Meta-Brain 在「参数-增益」trade-off \n      空间中占据了 VLA-GSE 和 FTM 之间的最优区间。\n      VLA-GSE 的 gain 数据直接引自原论文（Qwen3-VL-4B backbone 上 frozen 53.6%→81.2%，\n      gain=27.6%），跨 backbone 比较需在论文中注明 caveat。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Parameter efficiency comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Backbone\", \"Trainable Params\", \"Gain over Frozen\", \"Gain/M-param\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"FTM\", \"pi0\", \"4K\", 14.7, 3675.0]\n          - [\"Universal LoRA (r16)\", \"pi0\", \"2.0M\", 11.2, 5.60]\n          - [\"Meta-Brain\", \"pi0\", \"6.1M\", 24.8, 4.07]\n          - [\"Meta-Brain + CM\", \"pi0\", \"6.1M\", 27.2, 4.46]\n          - [\"VLA-GSE*\", \"Qwen3-VL-4B\", \"114M\", 27.6, 0.24]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot (Figure 5 in paper): x-axis = trainable params (log scale, 1K to 200M), y-axis = gain over frozen baseline (%). Points: FTM (bottom-left, high slope from origin), Universal LoRA (mid-left), Meta-Brain (mid, star marker), Meta-Brain+CM (mid, diamond), VLA-GSE (far right, asterisk with cross-backbone caveat). Pareto front line through FTM→Meta-Brain→VLA-GSE. Meta-Brain clearly on or near Pareto front. Dashed iso-efficiency lines (constant gain/M) for reference.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scatter plot 是 Claim 3 的视觉锚点。关键信息：在 log-scale x 轴上，\n      Meta-Brain 距 VLA-GSE 向左一个数量级以上，但 y 轴差距很小（24.8 vs 27.6）。\n      论文应在图注中明确 VLA-GSE 使用不同 backbone（Qwen3-VL-4B），\n      并引导读者关注 gain-over-own-baseline 指标而非绝对值。\n      Universal LoRA 的数据点是重要的 in-backbone 参照——它证明仅增加参数（从 2M 到 6M）\n      不如增加路由（从 universal 到 routed），因为 rank-48 universal LoRA 预期仍 ~67%。\n\n  - name: \"Correction Memory ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      Compare Meta-Brain with and without Correction Memory. CM modulates routing \n      weights via retrieved exemplars. Quantify marginal gain.\n    expected_results:\n      meta_brain_no_cm: 78.4\n      meta_brain_with_cm: 80.8\n      cm_ablation_delta: 2.4\n      cm_delta_camera: 2.0\n      cm_delta_light: 2.0\n      cm_delta_background: 2.0\n      cm_delta_noise: 4.0\n      cm_delta_layout: 2.0\n      cm_delta_robot: 3.0\n      cm_alpha_learned: 0.18\n      cm_retrieval_latency_ms: 0.8\n      cm_faiss_index_size_MB: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      CM 的 2.4% 增益来自两个机制：\n      (1) 路由权重精修：对于 PAR 不确定的样本（routing entropy 较高），\n      CM 从 FAISS 检索到的 k-NN exemplar 提供了基于历史成功案例的权重校准，\n      将这些 borderline 样本推向正确专家。noise 类型获益最大（+4.0%），\n      因为 sensor_noise 与 camera 扰动在激活空间中距离较近，PAR 在此区域\n      routing 不确定性最高，CM 的 exemplar matching 恰好能消除这一歧义。\n      (2) 校正强度调制：learned alpha=0.18 说明 CM 的权重修正幅度温和，\n      不会覆盖 PAR 的主信号，仅在需要时提供微调——这是「optional module」\n      定位的实验支撑。\n      CM 只增加 1 个可学习参数（alpha）+ CPU-bound FAISS 检索（0.8ms），\n      对推理延迟几乎无影响，使其成为一个低风险的即插即用模块。\n      2.4% gain 在 [1, 4] 范围内，足以在论文中报告但不构成核心贡献——\n      这恰好是理想定位：CM 是额外加分项而非系统必要组件。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"CM ablation per-perturbation\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"w/o CM\", \"w/ CM\", \"CM Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 72.0, 74.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"light\", 78.0, 80.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"background\", 76.0, 78.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"noise\", 70.0, 74.0, \"+4.0\"]\n          - [\"layout\", 88.0, 90.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"robot\", 86.0, 89.0, \"+3.0\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 78.4, 80.8, \"+2.4\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: w/ and w/o CM for each perturbation type. CM gains highlighted with delta annotations. Noise and robot types show largest improvements.\"\n      - \"Scatter: per-sample routing entropy (x) vs CM-induced weight change magnitude (y), showing CM intervenes most on high-entropy (uncertain) samples.\"\n    analysis: >\n      CM 对 reviewer concern C6 的回应很清晰：2.4% gain with 1 learned param, \n      0.8ms latency, 完全 optional。建议在论文中将 CM 放在 ablation section 而非 \n      main method，避免给审稿人造成「系统过于复杂」的印象。\n      noise 类型的 +4% 增益可以作为 case study 展示 CM 的工作机制。\n\n  - name: \"Router architecture comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      Compare PAR router variants: 2-layer MLP, linear classifier, attention-based. \n      All on PaliGemma layer 6. Measure routing accuracy and downstream success.\n    expected_results:\n      mlp_routing_acc: 97.2\n      mlp_downstream: 78.4\n      mlp_params_K: 48\n      linear_routing_acc: 94.1\n      linear_downstream: 76.6\n      linear_params_K: 6\n      attention_routing_acc: 97.8\n      attention_downstream: 78.8\n      attention_params_K: 196\n      mlp_vs_linear_downstream_gap: 1.8\n      mlp_vs_attention_downstream_gap: -0.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      三种路由器的性能梯度与 Phase 0 的分类难度分析一致：\n      (1) Linear (94.1% → 76.6%): 线性可分性已经很强（Phase 0 证实 layer 6 的类别边界\n      几乎线性），但 ~6% 的误差集中在 Visual 子类型间的边界区域（noise vs camera），\n      导致下游 1.8% 的性能损失。线性模型只有 6K params，极其轻量。\n      (2) MLP (97.2% → 78.4%): 两层 MLP 捕捉到非线性边界，将路由误差压缩到 2.8%，\n      在参数效率（48K）和性能间取得最佳平衡。48K 相对于 6M LoRA params 可忽略不计。\n      (3) Attention (97.8% → 78.8%): attention 机制可以利用 token 间关系进行路由，\n      略优于 MLP (+0.6% routing, +0.4% downstream)，但参数量增加 4x（196K），\n      增益不具统计显著性。\n      MLP 是论文默认选择的合理性得到验证：比 linear 明显好、与 attention 实质等价、\n      参数最经济。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Router architecture comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Router\", \"Params\", \"Routing Acc (%)\", \"Downstream (%)\", \"Δ vs MLP\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Linear\", \"6K\", 94.1, 76.6, \"-1.8\"]\n          - [\"2-layer MLP (default)\", \"48K\", 97.2, 78.4, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Attention-based\", \"196K\", 97.8, 78.8, \"+0.4\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Small dual-axis bar chart: routing accuracy (left axis) and downstream success (right axis) for 3 router types. Shows diminishing returns beyond MLP.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这个实验回答了一个隐含问题：路由器复杂度如何影响整体系统？\n      答案是：影响极小。94.1→97.2% 的路由精度提升带来 1.8% 下游增益，\n      但 97.2→97.8% 的进一步提升仅带来 0.4%。这是因为 Phase 0 分类本身很容易，\n      简单模型已足够——与 reviewer concern C1 的回应一致。\n      建议在 appendix 报告此结果，主文只提 MLP 作为默认配置。\n\n  - name: \"6-class vs 3-class routing comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      Compare 6-class fine-grained routing (6 LoRA experts) vs 3-class coarse routing \n      (3 experts). Test whether finer granularity justifies additional parameters.\n    expected_results:\n      three_class_overall: 78.4\n      three_class_params_M: 6.1\n      six_class_overall: 79.4\n      six_class_params_M: 12.2\n      marginal_gain: 1.0\n      marginal_gain_per_additional_expert: 0.33\n      six_class_camera: 74.0\n      six_class_light: 80.0\n      six_class_background: 78.0\n      six_class_noise: 74.0\n      six_class_layout: 88.0\n      six_class_robot: 82.0\n      six_class_routing_acc: 96.8\n      intra_visual_gain: 1.5\n      spatial_physical_gain: -0.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      6-class routing 仅带来 1.0% 的边际增益，原因：\n      (1) Phase 0 已显示 intra-Visual 子类型之间的特征距离远小于 inter-category 距离，\n      6-class 在 Visual 子类型间的路由精度（96.8%）略低于 3-class（97.2%），\n      说明更细的边界带来了更多的路由噪声；\n      (2) Visual 子类型的校正模式确实有差异（camera 需要修复 color/geometry 畸变，\n      noise 需要去噪平滑），所以 6 个专家在 Visual 上略优 (+1.5%)，\n      但这一增益被 spatial/physical 的轻微退化 (-0.7%) 部分抵消——\n      6-class 中 layout 和 robot 各自只有一个专家（与 3-class 相同），\n      但 router 增加了 4 个 Visual 类别输出后 softmax 分母增大，\n      导致 layout/robot 的 routing confidence 略降；\n      (3) 6 个 LoRA 专家的参数量翻倍（12.2M），但增益仅 1.0%，\n      gain/additional-param 极低（0.33%/expert vs 3-class 的 4.07 gain/M）。\n      结论：3-class taxonomy 在效率-性能 trade-off 上是最优粒度，\n      与 Phase 0 的 mechanistic 分析（early/mid/late layers 对应 Visual/Spatial/Physical）一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"6-class vs 3-class per-perturbation\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"3-class\", \"6-class\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"camera\", 72.0, 74.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"light\", 78.0, 80.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"background\", 76.0, 78.0, \"+2.0\"]\n          - [\"noise\", 70.0, 74.0, \"+4.0\"]\n          - [\"layout\", 88.0, 88.0, \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"robot\", 86.0, 82.0, \"-4.0\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 78.4, 79.4, \"+1.0\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 3-class vs 6-class per type. Visual types show small gains; robot shows slight regression. Annotations: total param cost for each configuration.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这个结果直接回应 reviewer concern C5（3-class 是否太粗）：\n      答案是「对当前任务集合，3-class 是 sweet spot」。论文应在 discussion 中 \n      承认 6-class 在某些 Visual 子类型上有额外区分度，但将 3-class 定位为 \n      Occam's razor 选择。robot 类的 -4% 退化值得关注——可能是因为 6 个 softmax \n      输出中 robot 的 prior probability 被稀释。如果 LIBERO-Plus 扩展更多物理扰动\n      子类型，6-class 或更细的 taxonomy 可能变得必要。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-backbone validation — OpenVLA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      Replicate Phase 0 + Phase 1 core pipeline on OpenVLA to test generalizability \n      of perturbation-diagnostic routing across architectures.\n    expected_results:\n      cross_backbone: \"OpenVLA (SigLIP + Llama-2-7B)\"\n      phase0_3class_f1: 0.972\n      phase0_best_layer: 8\n      phase0_pooling: \"mean\"\n      openvla_frozen_overall: 48.2\n      openvla_universal_lora_overall: 58.6\n      openvla_meta_brain_overall: 70.4\n      openvla_gain_over_frozen: 22.2\n      openvla_gain_over_universal: 11.8\n      openvla_oracle_overall: 71.8\n      openvla_oracle_par_gap: 1.4\n      openvla_routing_diagonality: 0.89\n    result_rationale: >\n      OpenVLA 上的复现确认 perturbation-diagnostic routing 是跨架构通用的：\n      (1) Phase 0 F1=0.972（略低于 pi0 的 0.993）：OpenVLA 使用 SigLIP（非 PaliGemma）\n      作为视觉编码器，最佳层从 layer 6 移至 layer 8，但分类精度依然极高。\n      这与 SAFE 论文在 OpenVLA 上的 probing 结果一致，进一步支持「VLA 内部表征 \n      普遍编码扰动类型信息」的核心假说。\n      (2) gain over frozen = 22.2%（pi0 上为 24.8%）：绝对增益略低，因为 OpenVLA \n      的 frozen baseline 更低（48.2% vs 53.6%），说明 OpenVLA 本身对扰动更脆弱，\n      校正难度更大。但 gain 仍在 best-tier 范围 [22, 28] 的低端。\n      (3) gain over universal = 11.8%（pi0 上为 13.6%）：路由增益在 OpenVLA 上 \n      同样显著，确认了 Claim 2 的跨架构有效性。\n      (4) Oracle-PAR gap = 1.4%（pi0 上为 1.2%）：略大但仍在 [0, 2] 内，\n      与 Phase 0 F1 略低（0.972 vs 0.993）一致。\n      OpenVLA 的较低绝对性能可归因于其较小的视觉编码器容量和不同的训练数据分布。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-backbone comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"pi0 (PaliGemma)\", \"OpenVLA (SigLIP)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Phase 0 3-class F1\", 0.993, 0.972]\n          - [\"Best probe layer\", 6, 8]\n          - [\"Frozen baseline (%)\", 53.6, 48.2]\n          - [\"Universal LoRA (%)\", 64.8, 58.6]\n          - [\"Meta-Brain (%)\", 78.4, 70.4]\n          - [\"Oracle (%)\", 79.6, 71.8]\n          - [\"Gain over frozen\", 24.8, 22.2]\n          - [\"Gain over universal\", 13.6, 11.8]\n          - [\"Oracle-PAR gap\", 1.2, 1.4]\n          - [\"Routing diagonality\", 0.92, 0.89]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side ablation ladder bars for pi0 and OpenVLA, showing parallel staircase pattern despite different absolute values. Gain-over-frozen annotations highlight comparable relative improvements.\"\n    analysis: >\n      跨 backbone 验证是应对 reviewer concern C3 的关键实验。\n      尽管绝对数值不同（OpenVLA 整体低 ~8%），增益模式高度一致：\n      universal→meta-brain 的 gain 在两个 backbone 上分别为 13.6% 和 11.8%，\n      routing diagonality 分别为 0.92 和 0.89——都远高于 random baseline (0.33)。\n      Phase 0 的最佳层从 layer 6 (PaliGemma) 移至 layer 8 (SigLIP) 符合预期：\n      不同视觉编码器的信息编码深度不同，但扰动类型信息的可提取性是通用的。\n      论文中应以 gain-over-baseline 为主要比较指标，避免直接对比绝对值。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA layer placement ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      Vary which PaliGemma layers receive LoRA. Test whether optimal layer placement \n      differs by perturbation type (early for Visual, mid for Spatial, late for Physical).\n    expected_results:\n      lora_v_early_2_8: 77.2\n      lora_v_mid_6_12: 72.8\n      lora_v_late_12_18: 68.4\n      lora_v_all: 76.0\n      lora_s_early_2_8: 82.0\n      lora_s_mid_6_12: 91.4\n      lora_s_late_12_18: 86.0\n      lora_s_all: 90.0\n      lora_p_early_2_8: 78.0\n      lora_p_mid_6_12: 82.0\n      lora_p_late_12_18: 89.2\n      lora_p_all: 88.0\n      optimal_v: \"early (layers 2-8)\"\n      optimal_s: \"mid (layers 6-12)\"\n      optimal_p: \"late (layers 12-18)\"\n      type_aligned_overall: 80.2\n      all_layers_overall: 78.4\n      type_aligned_gain_over_all_layers: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      层放置的最优分布与 VLA 处理扰动的 mechanistic 假设高度吻合：\n      (1) LoRA-V 最优在 early layers (2-8): Visual 扰动（camera/light/background/noise）\n      在视觉编码阶段损坏表征，early layers 是信号最先被破坏的地方，\n      在此处施加 LoRA 校正效率最高。LoRA-V 在 late layers 仅 68.4%（接近 universal LoRA），\n      因为视觉损坏在传播到高层后已经耦合到语义表征中，难以局部修复。\n      (2) LoRA-S 最优在 mid layers (6-12): Spatial 扰动改变物体空间关系，\n      这类信息在 mid layers 被编码为 spatial token relationships。\n      LoRA-S 在 mid layers 达 91.4%（超过 all-layers 的 90.0%），\n      说明集中校正比分散校正更有效——避免了 early/late layers 的无用更新。\n      (3) LoRA-P 最优在 late layers (12-18): Physical 扰动影响动力学属性，\n      这些信息在高层被整合为 action planning 信号。LoRA-P 在 late layers 达 89.2%。\n      Type-aligned 配置（每个专家放在最优层区间）比 all-layers 配置高 1.8%，\n      同时每个专家的参数量减少 ~60%（仅覆盖 6 层而非 18 层）。\n      这为更极致的参数效率提供了方向，但增加了系统复杂度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Layer placement × expert type (own-type success rate %)\"\n        columns: [\"Expert\", \"Early (2-8)\", \"Mid (6-12)\", \"Late (12-18)\", \"All layers\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA-V (Visual)\", 77.2, 72.8, 68.4, 76.0]\n          - [\"LoRA-S (Spatial)\", 82.0, 91.4, 86.0, 90.0]\n          - [\"LoRA-P (Physical)\", 78.0, 82.0, 89.2, 88.0]\n      - name: \"System-level layer placement comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Configuration\", \"Params/expert\", \"Visual\", \"Spatial\", \"Physical\", \"Overall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All layers (default)\", \"~2.0M\", 76.0, 90.0, 88.0, 78.4]\n          - [\"Type-aligned layers\", \"~0.8M\", 77.2, 91.4, 89.2, 80.2]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3×3 heatmap: expert rows × layer-group columns, cell values = own-type success rate. Clear diagonal pattern (V-early, S-mid, P-late) with highest values along the diagonal.\"\n    analysis: >\n      层放置 ablation 提供了 mechanistic insight 而非直接的系统设计改进。\n      对角模式（V-early, S-mid, P-late）与 VLA 的分层信息处理模型一致，\n      为 Phase 0 的单层分类结果提供了因果方向的支持：layer 6 能区分扰动类型，\n      因为不同类型的信息损坏恰好在该层汇聚/分离。\n      Type-aligned 配置带来 1.8% 增益和 60% 参数节省，但增加了工程复杂度\n      （需要为每个专家配置不同的层 mask）。建议在论文 appendix 中作为 \n      「进一步优化方向」报告，主系统保持 all-layers 的简洁配置。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"40703030-3e58-41b3-9b6d-2da547bf07b9","total_cost_usd":0.6959144999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11192,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":24552,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11192,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":24552,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11192,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11192},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6149,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006234,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":24552,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11192,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6896804999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"639e4f4d-8308-429c-beea-5f664d59eaa1"}
